\section{Main workflow (tier 1)}{

\enumerate{
\item Calibrate each cohort x domain: \code{\link[=kits_item]{kits_item()}} (the PCM, by default with dexter, plus the threshold of every step).
\item Cohort link (for example M36 -> M03), with the thresholds of the common items: \code{\link[=kits_linking]{kits_linking()}}.
\item Link to D, with the anchor items against the GSED difficulties: \code{\link[=kits_linking_d]{kits_linking_d()}}.
Several domains can share one line.
\item Person scores: \code{\link[=kits_subj]{kits_subj()}} (dexter's WLE; it can always be computed), with the waves and
ages of the person-waves in \code{persons}. Then theta on the reference scale =
\code{intercept + slope * theta} with the cohort link, and D = \code{intercept + slope * theta} with
the D link.
Without links (one cohort), \code{\link[=kits]{kits()}} calibrates and scores in one step; \code{plot()} gives a Wright map.
Raw-score to ability table of each wave: \code{s |> kits_subj_table()}.
\item Norms: screen the waves \code{\link[=kits_norm_screen]{kits_norm_screen()}}, set the age range \code{\link[=kits_norm_ages]{kits_norm_ages()}},
fit the continuous norm \code{\link[=kits_norms]{kits_norms()}} (cNORM shash; \verb{by =} one norm per group; \code{plot()} gives
the percentile curves), and get the same-age z \code{\link[=kits_norm_z]{kits_norm_z()}}.
\item Checks: item fit (kept as \code{item$itemfit} by \code{\link[=kits_item]{kits_item()}}; \code{\link[=kits_itemfit]{kits_itemfit()}} for other data)
and dexter's interaction model per wave \code{\link[=kits_inter]{kits_inter()}};
person fit (\code{infit}, \code{outfit} of \code{\link[=kits_subj]{kits_subj()}}); \code{plot()} of a link and of a norm.
}
}

